I pulled this off comp.archives:

----------------------------------------------------
From biss@ctss02.hydro.qc.ca (Sylvain Bissonnette)
Newsgroups: comp.archives
Subject: [sci.electronics] tools for the 68hc11
Date: 14 Jan 1994 11:16:03 +0100

Archive-Name: auto/sci.electronics/tools-for-the-68hc11

I developped two specific tools that could be very helpful for anyone working with the 68hc11, 6805, 6809,
etc... The first one is a package deal in which, by running one program named upam, it offers you

	text editor, assembler, communication software and more.

The second one provides you the possibility to program/erase the 68ch11 EEPROM by the boot load by running
the program bload11.

All these programs are working on PC stations. Both sources and executables are available by anonymous
ftp to ctss01.cct.hydro.qc.ca in directories pub/biss/upam and pub/biss/bload11.

Please, Email any suggestion to biss@cct.hydro.qc.ca

-----------------------------------------------------------

have fun!

Rick

